# AICL Spec: CogNet-AICL Integration Bridge
# The cognitive bridge that connects AICL structured specifications
# to CogNet's non-transformer cognitive engine for AGI synthesis.
# Written by an AI that read the grammar once and just... coded.

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 1 — Architecture (Mandatory)
# =============================================================================

Goal:
Bridge AICL specifications to CogNet cognitive engine, enabling structured architectural intent to drive non-transformer reasoning with hierarchical memory, cognitive routing, and compositional inference

Constraint:
AICL-to-CogNet translation must preserve semantic fidelity above 95%

Constraint:
Cognitive routing decisions must complete in O(n) time complexity

Constraint:
Memory retrieval latency must stay below 50ms for working memory and 200ms for episodic memory

Constraint:
Bridge must handle bidirectional translation: AICL spec to CogNet cognitive graph and CogNet reasoning output back to AICL validation

Constraint:
No transformer dependency anywhere in the pipeline

Risk:
Semantic drift during AICL-to-cognitive-graph translation

Recovery:
Apply proof-of-origin hash binding at each translation stage and validate semantic equivalence before committing

Risk:
CogNet memory overflow from large AICL specifications

Recovery:
Compress AICL layers into hierarchical memory chunks with semantic summarization and promote only active layers to working memory

Risk:
Cognitive routing bottleneck on complex multi-layer specs

Recovery:
Enable parallel cognitive routing across independent layers and fall back to sequential routing only on dependency conflicts

Risk:
Bidirectional translation asymmetry where CogNet output cannot map back to AICL constructs

Recovery:
Maintain translation ledger with original AICL AST references and generate synthetic AICL validation for unmapped outputs

Risk:
Compositional reasoner produces incoherent bindings across distant AICL entities

Recovery:
Apply hyperdimensional binding coherence check and reject bindings below similarity threshold with diagnostic output

Layer:
AICL Parser Bridge
    Sublayer:
    Spec ingestion
    Sublayer:
    AST normalization
    Sublayer:
    Semantic extraction
    Sublayer:
    Proof-of-origin binding

Layer:
Cognitive Graph Builder
    Sublayer:
    Entity-to-concept mapping
    Sublayer:
    Behavior-to-procedure encoding
    Sublayer:
    Risk-to-anticipation wiring
    Sublayer:
    Layer-to-hierarchy construction

Layer:
CogNet Engine Interface
    Sublayer:
    Cognitive router
    Sublayer:
    Working memory controller
    Sublayer:
    Episodic memory controller
    Sublayer:
    Semantic memory controller
    Sublayer:
    Compositional reasoner

Layer:
Reasoning Output Translator
    Sublayer:
    Cognitive-to-AICL mapping
    Sublayer:
    Validation synthesis
    Sublayer:
    Confidence scoring
    Sublayer:
    Explanation generator

Layer:
Feedback Loop
    Sublayer:
    Reasoning-to-spec refinement
    Sublayer:
    Pattern learning from compilation outcomes
    Sublayer:
    Autonomous spec improvement
    Sublayer:
    Self-correction propagation

Validation:
AICL specification compiles to valid CogNet cognitive graph with zero semantic loss on core constructs

Validation:
CogNet reasoning output translates back to AICL-compliant validation statements

Validation:
Cognitive routing handles 10-layer spec in under 100ms

Validation:
Memory hierarchy correctly promotes and demotes AICL layers based on reasoning context

Validation:
Proof of origin is preserved end-to-end from AICL source through CogNet reasoning and back

Validation:
Bidirectional translation round-trip preserves semantic intent above 95% fidelity

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 2 — Entities
# =============================================================================

Entity AICLSpec
    spec_id: string
    goal: string
    constraints: list
    risks: list
    recoveries: list
    layers: list
    validations: list
    proof_hash: string
    source_path: string
    compiled_at: datetime

Entity CognitiveNode
    node_id: string
    concept: string
    node_type: string
    embedding: list
    confidence: float
    source_spec_id: string
    source_line: integer
    memory_tier: string
    created_at: datetime
    access_count: integer

Entity CognitiveEdge
    edge_id: string
    source_node: string
    target_node: string
    relation: string
    weight: float
    binding_type: string
    provenance_hash: string

Entity ReasoningTrace
    trace_id: string
    spec_id: string
    reasoning_steps: list
    route_path: list
    memory_accessed: list
    compositional_bindings: list
    confidence: float
    duration_ms: float
    completed_at: datetime

Entity TranslationLedger
    entry_id: string
    direction: string
    source_hash: string
    target_hash: string
    semantic_fidelity: float
    aicl_construct: string
    cognet_construct: string
    verified: boolean
    timestamp: datetime

Entity MemoryChunk
    chunk_id: string
    content: dict
    tier: string
    compression: string
    reference_spec: string
    reference_layer: string
    access_frequency: integer
    last_accessed: datetime
    promotion_score: float

Entity ProvenanceBinding
    binding_id: string
    aicl_hash: string
    cognet_hash: string
    stage: string
    verification_count: integer
    verified: boolean
    created_at: datetime

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 3 — Behaviors
# =============================================================================

Behavior ParseAndExtract
    Input:
        AICLSpec raw_spec
    Output:
        CognitiveNode extracted_concepts
        CognitiveEdge extracted_relations
        TranslationLedger ledger_entries
    Action:
        parse AICL source into normalized AST
        extract entities as cognitive concept nodes
        extract behaviors as procedural edges
        extract risks as anticipation nodes with recovery links
        extract layers as hierarchy structure
        bind proof-of-origin hash to each extracted element
        record translation ledger entries for each mapping

Behavior BuildCognitiveGraph
    Input:
        CognitiveNode concepts
        CognitiveEdge relations
        list layer_hierarchy
    Output:
        dict cognitive_graph
        dict hierarchy_map
    Action:
        organize concept nodes into cognitive graph structure
        wire procedural edges between behavior nodes
        construct hierarchical layer mapping for memory tiering
        apply hyperdimensional encoding to node embeddings
        validate graph connectivity and reachability
        return complete cognitive graph ready for CogNet engine

Behavior RouteCognition
    Input:
        string query_concept
        dict cognitive_graph
        dict routing_config
    Output:
        list route_path
        list memory_access_plan
        float estimated_latency
    Action:
        identify query concept in cognitive graph
        compute O(n) cognitive route through relevant subgraph
        determine memory tier access sequence
        select working vs episodic vs semantic memory
        estimate total reasoning latency
        return route with memory access plan

Behavior ComposeReasoning
    Input:
        list route_path
        dict cognitive_graph
        MemoryChunk active_context
    Output:
        ReasoningTrace reasoning_result
        list compositional_bindings
    Action:
        traverse cognitive route path
        at each node retrieve relevant memory chunks
        apply compositional reasoner to bind related concepts
        check binding coherence via hyperdimensional similarity
        accumulate reasoning steps into trace
        compute overall confidence score
        return reasoning trace with bindings

Behavior TranslateBackToAICL
    Input:
        ReasoningTrace reasoning_output
        TranslationLedger original_ledger
    Output:
        string aicl_validation
        float semantic_fidelity
        list explanation_steps
    Action:
        map reasoning output nodes back to AICL constructs via ledger
        synthesize AICL validation statements from reasoning conclusions
        compute semantic fidelity of round-trip translation
        generate human-readable explanation of reasoning path
        if fidelity below threshold flag for human review
        return AICL validation with confidence and explanation

Behavior RefineSpecFromReasoning
    Input:
        ReasoningTrace reasoning_trace
        AICLSpec original_spec
        dict pattern_history
    Output:
        AICLSpec refined_spec
        list improvements_applied
        dict learned_patterns
    Action:
        analyze reasoning trace for inefficiencies or failures
        identify AICL spec elements that caused routing confusion
        propose refined constraints risks or layer structure
        apply autonomous corrections where confidence is high
        flag uncertain improvements for human review
        update pattern learning database
        return refined spec with change log

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 4 — Conditions
# =============================================================================

Condition:

When semantic fidelity drops below 90 percent on translation

Then halt pipeline and invoke human review with diagnostic report showing exact drift points

Condition:

When cognitive routing encounters cyclic dependency between layers

Then detect cycle and break at lowest-confidence edge then reroute and log cycle detection

Condition:

When compositional binding coherence score falls below threshold

Then reject binding and attempt alternative composition path or decompose into simpler sub-bindings

Condition:

When working memory exceeds capacity during reasoning

Then compress least-accessed chunks to episodic tier and promote only active chunks to working memory

Condition:

When proof-of-origin verification fails at any stage

Then halt translation and quarantine affected nodes and alert integrity verification system

Condition:

When CogNet reasoning produces output that cannot map to any AICL construct

Then create synthetic AICL validation entry and flag as novel inference requiring human classification

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 5 — Events
# =============================================================================

Event:

On spec ingestion complete

Action:
    validate AICL syntax and bind initial proof-of-origin hash and begin cognitive graph construction

Event:

On cognitive graph built

Action:
    verify graph connectivity and tier memory assignments and emit graph statistics for monitoring

Event:

On reasoning step completed

Action:
    update working memory and log trace step and check confidence threshold and emit progress heartbeat

Event:

On translation round-trip complete

Action:
    compute semantic fidelity score and verify proof-of-origin chain and emit quality metrics

Event:

On spec refinement applied

Action:
    re-verify refined spec against original goal and update pattern database and propagate changes to dependent layers

Event:

On novel inference detected

Action:
    create synthetic AICL validation and flag for human review and store in episodic memory for future reference

